# Example vocabulary

## Namespaces
### Ontology Base URI
prefix :                <https://example.org/ns/>
prefix id:              <https://example.org/id/>

### Core W3C ontologies (OWL 2 reserved vocabulary)
prefix rdf:             <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
prefix rdfs:            <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
prefix owl:             <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
prefix xsd:             <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>


### Object Properties
:ancestor
    a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    owl:inverseOf :descendant ;
    rdfs:label "has ancestor"@en ;
.

:child
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :descendant ;
    rdfs:domain :Parent ;
    rdfs:range :Child ;
    rdfs:label "has child"@en ;
.

:descendant
    a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    owl:inverseOf :ancestor ;
    rdfs:label "has descendant"@en ;
.

:parent
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy : ;
    owl:inverseOf :child ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf :ancestor ;
    rdfs:domain :Child ;
    rdfs:range :Parent ;
    rdfs:label "has parent"@en ;
.

id:x :child id:y .
id:y :child id:z .
